Dear Mr Moss,

We are still waiting for your decision on the entrance door at 14 Lantern Mews, so I am sending the request again with a new update.

New information: the building manager at Brindlewick Court says a common-area check last month noted this flat entrance door as closing slowly. The checker did not measure any gap or inspect the door set, and the building office has no individual report or certification record for it. He asks to be consulted before any changes to the door or its hardware. This fits what the tenant reports, that the door catches near the top, and what the contractor saw, that the door touches the frame at the top. The building file lists the flat entrance doors as fire-resisting. The cause of the catching is still unknown.

You asked whether this could be limited to decorating. On what we know, we cannot say that. The painting quote (Pale Finch Decorating, ref NBL-017-Q1, £186.00) covers painting only. It does not cover the catching and gives no opinion on the door's fire rating.

Please tell us which option you would like:
(A) Painting only, £186.00.
(B) A further inspection by a door specialist of the closing, clearances and hinges, and of the fire-resisting status. We would send you the price before any work, and building management would be consulted first.
(C) Both, in sequence.

Nothing will be booked or spent until you approve. The contractor has not yet told us whether his visit carries a charge. We will tell you if it does, and no cost was approved beforehand, so payment for it will be your decision.

Kind regards,
Northbridge Lettings
